      "obligations": ["XIV-13"],
      "derivation": "The second of the two news a migration sends, driven here for the same reason the arrival above is: **it is what tells this door its own roads.** Where a warden's published hints live is Article II's — \"the two records name the facts a warden must keep, never how it keeps them\" — and a kit whose roads are named per act by its host conforms exactly as one that stores them does. So the word this door points with is complete only once the arrival has been announced, and a scenario that asked `moved` before it would be asserting one kit's storage rather than the law. **The migration scenario drives this same news and this one repeats it**, because the exchanges after it are unreachable without it and an exchange that asserted nothing would be a hole in the middle of a scenario.",
